IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er4-nouns`
IMPORT `er4-part3-1-entitlement`

-- Tests of regs 76.09 to 76.18, 76.22 and 76.23 (SOR-96-332.txt lines 1215-1279). Every expected value is written by hand
-- from the text. Dates and amounts are invented for the tests; "the day on which this Part comes into force" is an
-- input that the text does not give, so 1 January 2020 below is an invented day, not the real one.

§ `Reg 76.09(2) and (1) -- disentitlement to benefits under section 22 or 23`

-- (2) needs both the claimant's request and the Commission's finding that the provincial amount is not substantially equivalent.
#ASSERT `reg 76.09(2) subsection (1) does not apply` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.09(2) subsection (1) does not apply` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.09(2) subsection (1) does not apply` TRUE FALSE
-- (1): entitled to provincial benefits, and (2) not applying: disentitled.
#ASSERT `reg 76.09(1) the claimant is disentitled to be paid benefits under section 22 or 23 of the Act` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.09(1) the claimant is disentitled to be paid benefits under section 22 or 23 of the Act` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.09(1) the claimant is disentitled to be paid benefits under section 22 or 23 of the Act` FALSE FALSE

§ `Reg 76.09(3) -- a week of other Part I or fishing benefits`

#ASSERT `reg 76.09(3) the claimant is disentitled to be paid those benefits in respect of the same week` `er4 other benefits under Part I of the Act` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 76.09(3) the claimant is disentitled to be paid those benefits in respect of the same week` `er4 other benefits under Part I of the Act` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 76.09(3) the claimant is disentitled to be paid those benefits in respect of the same week` `er4 benefits under the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 76.09(3) the claimant is disentitled to be paid those benefits in respect of the same week` `er4 benefits under the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Sections 22 and 23 are excluded from (3), whatever the week: (1) governs them.
#ASSERT `reg 76.09(3) the claimant is disentitled to be paid those benefits in respect of the same week` `er4 benefits under section 22 of the Act` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 76.09(3) the claimant is disentitled to be paid those benefits in respect of the same week` `er4 benefits under section 23 of the Act` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Anything else (e.g. Part VII.1 benefits): the subsection says nothing.
#ASSERT `reg 76.09(3) the claimant is disentitled to be paid those benefits in respect of the same week` `er4 benefits of another kind` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Reg 76.09(4) -- moving province changes nothing`

#ASSERT `reg 76.09(4) subsections (1) to (3) apply to the claimant whether or not they have ceased to reside in the province where the plan was established` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.09(4) subsections (1) to (3) apply to the claimant whether or not they have ceased to reside in the province where the plan was established` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.09(4) subsections (1) to (3) apply to the claimant whether or not they have ceased to reside in the province where the plan was established` FALSE TRUE

§ `Reg 76.09(5) -- the other person caring for the same child`

#ASSERT `reg 76.09(5)(a) subsections (1) to (3) apply in respect of the other person` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.09(5)(a) subsections (1) to (3) apply in respect of the other person` FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.09(5)(a) subsections (1) to (3) apply in respect of the other person` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.09(5)(a) subsections (1) to (3) apply in respect of the other person` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 76.09(5)(b) subsections 76.36(1) to (3) apply in respect of the other person` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.09(5)(b) subsections 76.36(1) to (3) apply in respect of the other person` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.09(5)(b) subsections 76.36(1) to (3) apply in respect of the other person` TRUE FALSE TRUE

§ `Reg 76.11 -- insured participant`

-- Arguments: already an insured participant under s 58, requests assistance, unemployed when requesting, has a benefit
-- period under a provincial plan, day that period ended (if it has), day of the request, would have been entitled to special benefits.
#ASSERT `reg 76.11 the person is an insured participant, as the definition in section 58 of the Act is adapted` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING (YMD 2026 6 30) FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 76.11 the person is an insured participant, as the definition in section 58 of the Act is adapted` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE NOTHING (YMD 2026 6 30) TRUE
-- Benefit period ended within the previous 60 months: ended 1 July 2021 (60 months later is 1 July 2026, on or after the request).
#ASSERT `reg 76.11 the person is an insured participant, as the definition in section 58 of the Act is adapted` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2021 7 1)) (YMD 2026 6 30) TRUE
-- Exactly 60 months before the request: still within it.
#ASSERT `reg 76.11 the person is an insured participant, as the definition in section 58 of the Act is adapted` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2021 6 30)) (YMD 2026 6 30) TRUE
-- One day more than 60 months: not within it.
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.11 the person is an insured participant, as the definition in section 58 of the Act is adapted` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2021 6 29)) (YMD 2026 6 30) TRUE
-- No benefit period under a provincial plan at all.
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.11 the person is an insured participant, as the definition in section 58 of the Act is adapted` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE NOTHING (YMD 2026 6 30) TRUE
-- Each other condition is needed.
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.11 the person is an insured participant, as the definition in section 58 of the Act is adapted` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE NOTHING (YMD 2026 6 30) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.11 the person is an insured participant, as the definition in section 58 of the Act is adapted` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE NOTHING (YMD 2026 6 30) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.11 the person is an insured participant, as the definition in section 58 of the Act is adapted` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE NOTHING (YMD 2026 6 30) FALSE

§ `Reg 76.13 -- a week of provincial benefits is a week in receipt of benefits`

#ASSERT `reg 76.13 the week is a week during which the person was in receipt of benefits, for subsection 8(5) of the Act` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 76.13 the week is a week during which the person was in receipt of benefits, for subsection 8(5) of the Act` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.13 the week is a week during which the person was in receipt of benefits, for subsection 8(5) of the Act` FALSE FALSE

§ `Reg 76.14 and 76.15 -- extension of the benefit period`

-- (a) Provincial benefits paid for pregnancy or the care of a new-born count like those under the Act; no other reason.
#ASSERT `reg 76.14(a) the benefits count as benefits paid for one of the reasons mentioned in paragraphs 12(3)(a) and (b) of the Act` `pregnancy` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 76.14(a) the benefits count as benefits paid for one of the reasons mentioned in paragraphs 12(3)(a) and (b) of the Act` `caring for a new-born or adopted child` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.14(a) the benefits count as benefits paid for one of the reasons mentioned in paragraphs 12(3)(a) and (b) of the Act` `pregnancy` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.14(a) the benefits count as benefits paid for one of the reasons mentioned in paragraphs 12(3)(a) and (b) of the Act` `a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine` TRUE TRUE
-- (b) The extension is up to the applicable maximum for a reason in paragraphs 12(3)(c) to (f); the figures here (26, 26, 35, 15 and a total of 50)
-- are the Act's own s 12(3) and s 12(5) figures, taken from the Act as cross-references and fed in as inputs.
#ASSERT `reg 76.14(b) the number of weeks up to which the benefit period is extended so that those benefits may be paid` `a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine` 26 50 EQUALS 26
#ASSERT `reg 76.14(b) the number of weeks up to which the benefit period is extended so that those benefits may be paid` `care or support of a family member` 26 50 EQUALS 26
#ASSERT `reg 76.14(b) the number of weeks up to which the benefit period is extended so that those benefits may be paid` `care or support of a critically ill child` 35 50 EQUALS 35
#ASSERT `reg 76.14(b) the number of weeks up to which the benefit period is extended so that those benefits may be paid` `care or support of a critically ill adult` 15 50 EQUALS 15
-- A reason in (a) or (b) of s 12(3) is not one the adapted words reach: the total stands.
#ASSERT `reg 76.14(b) the number of weeks up to which the benefit period is extended so that those benefits may be paid` `pregnancy` 15 50 EQUALS 50
-- 76.15: hospitalized child.
#ASSERT `reg 76.15 the number of weeks by which the benefit period is considered to be extended under subsection 10(12) of the Act` TRUE 3 EQUALS JUST 3
#ASSERT `reg 76.15 the number of weeks by which the benefit period is considered to be extended under subsection 10(12) of the Act` FALSE 3 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Reg 76.16 and 76.17 -- reduction of benefits`

#ASSERT `reg 76.16 the benefits payable under section 22 or 23 of the Act for the week are to be reduced` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.16 the benefits payable under section 22 or 23 of the Act for the week are to be reduced` FALSE
-- 400 payable, 150 of provincial benefits for the same week: 250.
#ASSERT `reg 76.17 the benefits payable under section 22 or 23 of the Act for the week after the provincial benefits are deducted` 400 150 EQUALS JUST 250
-- Deducting exactly what is payable leaves nothing; deducting more is not answered by the text.
#ASSERT `reg 76.17 the benefits payable under section 22 or 23 of the Act for the week after the provincial benefits are deducted` 150 150 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `reg 76.17 the benefits payable under section 22 or 23 of the Act for the week after the provincial benefits are deducted` 100 150 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Reg 76.18 -- no double counting of weeks`

#ASSERT `reg 76.18 a week of benefits paid under section 22 or 23 of the Act may be taken into account for that same purpose` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.18 a week of benefits paid under section 22 or 23 of the Act may be taken into account for that same purpose` TRUE

§ `Reg 76.22 -- the waiting period`

#ASSERT `reg 76.22 the condition of paragraph 40(6)(b), as adapted, is met` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 76.22 the condition of paragraph 40(6)(b), as adapted, is met` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.22 the condition of paragraph 40(6)(b), as adapted, is met` FALSE FALSE

§ `Reg 76.23 -- transition`

-- A birth the day before the invented in-force day, 1 January 2020: the Act applies. On the day itself: (a) does not.
#ASSERT `reg 76.23(a) the Act applies in respect of a claim for benefits made in respect of the birth or placement` (YMD 2019 12 31) (YMD 2020 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.23(a) the Act applies in respect of a claim for benefits made in respect of the birth or placement` (YMD 2020 1 1) (YMD 2020 1 1)
-- (b) At least one week paid before that day.
#ASSERT `reg 76.23(b) the Act continues to apply in respect of any claim relating to the birth or placement` 1
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.23(b) the Act continues to apply in respect of any claim relating to the birth or placement` 0
#ASSERT `reg 76.23 the Act applies to the claim as it did before this Part` (YMD 2019 12 31) (YMD 2020 1 1) 0
#ASSERT `reg 76.23 the Act applies to the claim as it did before this Part` (YMD 2020 3 1) (YMD 2020 1 1) 2
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.23 the Act applies to the claim as it did before this Part` (YMD 2020 3 1) (YMD 2020 1 1) 0
